{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"core gameplay loop core gameplay loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md","fileName":"Core Gameplay Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Core Gameplay Loop","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Interactivity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interactivity","Player Goal","Progression System","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"core gameplay loop core gameplay loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md","fileName":"Core Gameplay Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Core Gameplay Loop","heading":"Core Gameplay Loop","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A core gameplay loop is the interactive cycle central to the player's attention: intention leads to action, the game state changes, feedback communicates the result, and progress or reward informs the next intention.\n\nCore does not necessarily mean fastest or innermost. A game may shift among several core loops and nest rapid loops inside slower outer loops, connecting moment-to-moment play with [[Player Goal|goals]], learning, and [[Progression System|progression]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interactivity","Player Goal","Progression System","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Core Gameplay Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"core gameplay loop core gameplay loop","filePat